<title>USA: FGIC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co. said it has qualified for bond insuarance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Schaumburg Township, Ill., $8.1 million library general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--New Orleans, La.,  $30 million sewage service revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Hempstead Village, N.Y., $5.410 million various purpose bonds and $3.344 million various purpose bonds.</p>
<p>--Naples CSD, N.Y., $5.4 million school district GOs.</p>
<p>--Ontario, N.Y., $9.975 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Newberg, Oregon, $2.950 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Lebanon, Tenn., $2.8 million public improvement GOs.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
